\label{conj:PS}
Every connected subcubic graph other than $K_4$ admits a rich-neighbor
$5$-edge-coloring.

\label{lem:path-sequence}
Let $P=x_0x_1\cdots x_\ell$ be a path with $\ell\ge 4$ edges, and write $e_i=x_{i-1}x_i$ for $i\in[\ell]$. For any $a,b\in[5]$, the path $P$ has a strong $5$-edge-coloring $\psi$ satisfying
$\psi(e_1)=a$ and  $\psi(e_\ell)=b.$

\label{lem:star-forest}
Every component of $G'_F$ is a star, and no two edges of $F$ are
parallel.

\label{lem:port-list1}
The graph \(Q\) has a proper edge-coloring \(\psi\) such that
\(\psi(e)\in L(e)\) for every \(e\in E(Q)\).
